    "dish": {
      "word": "DISH",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "A vessel, as a platter, a plate, a bowl, used for serving up food at the table. She brought forth butter in a lordly dish. Judg. v. 25.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The food served in a dish; hence, any particular kind of food; as, a cold dish; a warm dish; a delicious dish. \"A dish fit for the gods.\" Shak. Home-home dishes that drive one from home. Hood.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The state of being concave, or like a dish, or the degree of such concavity; as, the dish of a wheel.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A hollow place, as in a field. Ogilvie.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Mining) (a) A trough about 28 inches long, 4 deep, and 6 wide, in which ore is measured. (b) That portion of the produce of a mine which is paid to the land owner or proprietor.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To put in a dish, ready for the table.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To make concave, or depress in the middle, like a dish; as, to dish a wheel by inclining the spokes.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To frustrate; to beat; to ruin. [Low] To dish out.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To serve out of a dish; to distribute in portions at table.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Arch.) To hollow out, as a gutter in stone or wood. dishes to be served at table.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
